WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.280
<v Beezle Wheezelby>The Ring, the Rats, and the Gold Beneath
the Earth.<break time="1.6s"/>

00:00:05.358 --> 00:00:11.358
<v Beezle Wheezelby>A Chronicle of the Adventurers of Fornost
| October 25–30.

00:00:11.866 --> 00:00:18.007
<v Beezle Wheezelby>There are tales of great heroes who set
forth to challenge ancient evils, restore

00:00:18.007 --> 00:00:23.226
<v Beezle Wheezelby>fallen kingdoms, and bring light to the
darkest corners of the world.

00:00:23.676 --> 00:00:26.636
<v Beezle Wheezelby>This is not quite one of those tales.

00:00:27.049 --> 00:00:32.538
<v Beezle Wheezelby>For this tale begins with three wolf
pups, a handful of hired swords, and a

00:00:32.538 --> 00:00:35.209
<v Beezle Wheezelby>rather unfortunate horse named Fred.

00:00:35.725 --> 00:00:41.465
<v Beezle Wheezelby><break time="0.9s"/>Part I: The Wolves of
Fornost.<break time="1.4s"/>

00:00:41.581 --> 00:00:46.326
<v Beezle Wheezelby>In the waning hours of an autumn
afternoon, a company of adventurers

00:00:46.326 --> 00:00:51.426
<v Beezle Wheezelby>departed the town of Fornost, bound for a
wolf den hidden deep within the

00:00:51.426 --> 00:00:52.701
<v Beezle Wheezelby>surrounding woods.

00:00:53.183 --> 00:00:58.786
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Their purpose was simple enough: capture
the young wolves and sell them for coin.

00:00:58.786 --> 00:01:04.109
<v Beezle Wheezelby>It was, by all appearances, a modest
undertaking. Yet those who have wandered

00:01:04.109 --> 00:01:09.572
<v Beezle Wheezelby>long upon the roads of this world know
that modest undertakings have a peculiar

00:01:09.572 --> 00:01:11.743
<v Beezle Wheezelby>habit of becoming anything but.

00:01:12.229 --> 00:01:17.317
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Among the company rode Sigurd, a
formidable warrior whose great strength

00:01:17.317 --> 00:01:22.906
<v Beezle Wheezelby>was matched only by his enthusiasm for
danger. Beside him traveled his faithful

00:01:22.906 --> 00:01:28.710
<v Beezle Wheezelby>war dog and the mercenary Karl. There was
also Alok, a ranger well acquainted with

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:34.371
<v Beezle Wheezelby>the wilderness, and Sulde, a cleric whose
talents and inclinations were somewhat

00:01:34.371 --> 00:01:35.589
<v Beezle Wheezelby>less predictable.

00:01:36.082 --> 00:01:40.674
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Two mounted crossbowmen joined the
expedition, having survived an earlier

00:01:40.674 --> 00:01:45.522
<v Beezle Wheezelby>adventure in the company's service. Their
confidence in these adventurers had

00:01:45.522 --> 00:01:50.242
<v Beezle Wheezelby>evidently survived as well, though one
would soon have cause to reconsider.

00:01:50.792 --> 00:01:55.862
<v Beezle Wheezelby>By evening, the party reached the
familiar gully where Alok had once laid

00:01:55.862 --> 00:02:01.425
<v Beezle Wheezelby>traps for wolves. The ranger crept ahead
to survey the den, hoping to repeat his

00:02:01.425 --> 00:02:02.552
<v Beezle Wheezelby>earlier success.

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:08.220
<v Beezle Wheezelby>But fate, that most mischievous of
companions, had other plans.

00:02:08.692 --> 00:02:13.010
<v Beezle Wheezelby>As Alok approached the ridge, he
stumbled, scattering his belongings

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:17.199
<v Beezle Wheezelby>across the ground. Before he could
recover, a wolf sprang from the

00:02:17.199 --> 00:02:17.972
<v Beezle Wheezelby>undergrowth.

00:02:18.491 --> 00:02:24.891
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Steel was drawn. Sigurd charged with his
hound, and the beast was quickly slain.

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:28.140
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Yet the forest had not finished with
them.

00:02:28.555 --> 00:02:34.539
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Two more wolves burst from cover and fell
upon the horses below. In the confusion,

00:02:34.539 --> 00:02:40.079
<v Beezle Wheezelby>one of the animals was struck down. Its
name was Fred, and its rider grieved

00:02:40.079 --> 00:02:45.250
<v Beezle Wheezelby>bitterly for him. Sigurd offered to
purchase another horse, but the man

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:46.875
<v Beezle Wheezelby>wanted no replacement.

00:02:47.314 --> 00:02:53.874
<v Beezle Wheezelby>For friendship, even between man and
beast, is not so easily measured in gold.

00:02:54.344 --> 00:02:59.733
<v Beezle Wheezelby>It was then that Sulde revealed the true
nature of a curious golden ring he had

00:02:59.733 --> 00:03:05.260
<v Beezle Wheezelby>acquired on an earlier adventure. Having
paid a considerable sum to a learned man

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:10.580
<v Beezle Wheezelby>for its identification, he had discovered
that the ring possessed the power to

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:12.584
<v Beezle Wheezelby>command the minds of mammals.

00:03:12.999 --> 00:03:18.858
<v Beezle Wheezelby>And so, with the wolves still feasting
upon their fallen quarry, Sulde bent

00:03:18.858 --> 00:03:20.679
<v Beezle Wheezelby>their wills to his own.

00:03:21.022 --> 00:03:26.920
<v Beezle Wheezelby>At his command, the beasts ceased their
attack and rolled upon the ground like

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:28.222
<v Beezle Wheezelby>obedient puppies.

00:03:28.679 --> 00:03:30.839
<v Beezle Wheezelby>The fighting was over.

00:03:31.242 --> 00:03:36.755
<v Beezle Wheezelby>With the wolves under his power, Sulde
led the company to the den, where three

00:03:36.755 --> 00:03:42.411
<v Beezle Wheezelby>young pups were discovered. The little
creatures were gathered into sacks, while

00:03:42.411 --> 00:03:47.995
<v Beezle Wheezelby>the company searched the dark hollow for
treasure. They found only bones, dirt,

00:03:47.995 --> 00:03:51.002
<v Beezle Wheezelby>and the remnants of lives already
consumed.

00:03:51.516 --> 00:03:57.066
<v Beezle Wheezelby>As for the two adult wolves, Sulde
considered whether they might be tamed.

00:03:57.066 --> 00:04:02.691
<v Beezle Wheezelby>But the ways of wild beasts are not
easily changed, and such an undertaking

00:04:02.691 --> 00:04:05.276
<v Beezle Wheezelby>promised years of uncertain labor.

00:04:05.782 --> 00:04:08.262
<v Beezle Wheezelby>He chose a swifter solution.

00:04:08.659 --> 00:04:12.099
<v Beezle Wheezelby>The wolves were commanded to destroy one
another.

00:04:12.476 --> 00:04:18.088
<v Beezle Wheezelby>It was an efficient end, though not one
upon which all companions looked with

00:04:18.088 --> 00:04:19.196
<v Beezle Wheezelby>equal approval.

00:04:19.663 --> 00:04:25.322
<v Beezle Wheezelby>That night, the company camped upon the
ridge. And when the darkness began to

00:04:25.322 --> 00:04:29.343
<v Beezle Wheezelby>yield to morning, a mournful howl rose
from the forest.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:32.280
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Other wolves had returned.

00:04:32.678 --> 00:04:38.438
<v Beezle Wheezelby>They found their den emptied, their kin
slain, and their young taken.

00:04:38.898 --> 00:04:44.316
<v Beezle Wheezelby>The adventurers searched the trees but
saw nothing. Still, as they made their

00:04:44.316 --> 00:04:49.378
<v Beezle Wheezelby>way toward Fornost, the distant howling
followed them through the woods.

00:04:49.925 --> 00:04:54.823
<v Beezle Wheezelby>By morning they had returned to town,
where the three pups were sold to a dog

00:04:54.823 --> 00:04:59.205
<v Beezle Wheezelby>breeder for thirty gold pieces. The wolf
pelts brought a little more.

00:04:59.724 --> 00:05:02.444
<v Beezle Wheezelby>A modest profit, one might say.

00:05:02.914 --> 00:05:07.881
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Though Fred, had he been capable of
expressing an opinion, might have

00:05:07.881 --> 00:05:09.634
<v Beezle Wheezelby>disputed the accounting.

00:05:10.022 --> 00:05:16.642
<v Beezle Wheezelby><break time="0.9s"/>Part II: Seven Rats
and Eight Dwarves.<break time="1.4s"/>

00:05:16.688 --> 00:05:20.670
<v Beezle Wheezelby>With their wolf-hunting venture
concluded, the company turned its

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:23.408
<v Beezle Wheezelby>attention to a matter of greater
consequence.

00:05:23.901 --> 00:05:29.136
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Word had reached them of dwarven miners
operating in secret beneath the lands of

00:05:29.136 --> 00:05:34.371
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Lord Guthrie. Gold was being taken from
the earth without the lord's permission,

00:05:34.371 --> 00:05:39.540
<v Beezle Wheezelby>and there were whispers of a kingdom in
the northwestern mountains whose agents

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:41.661
<v Beezle Wheezelby>had established hidden outposts.

00:05:42.085 --> 00:05:46.245
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Sigurd and Sulde entertained a bold idea.

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:52.420
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Why merely uncover the mines when one
might—seize—the operation itself?!

00:05:52.906 --> 00:05:58.025
<v Beezle Wheezelby>They resolved to seek miners and men
capable of working the excavations once

00:05:58.025 --> 00:06:00.346
<v Beezle Wheezelby>the intruders had been driven out.

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:06.285
<v Beezle Wheezelby>And so began what should have been an
uneventful search through the streets of

00:06:06.285 --> 00:06:06.850
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Fornost.

00:06:07.227 --> 00:06:10.507
<v Beezle Wheezelby>It did not remain uneventful for long.

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:16.011
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Down a narrow alley, the party
encountered seven giant rats—each nearly

00:06:16.011 --> 00:06:21.734
<v Beezle Wheezelby>the size of a small dog. The creatures
were feeding upon the refuse of the town,

00:06:21.734 --> 00:06:23.980
<v Beezle Wheezelby>bothering no one in particular.

00:06:24.448 --> 00:06:27.728
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Sulde, however, saw opportunity.

00:06:28.239 --> 00:06:34.090
<v Beezle Wheezelby>With his enchanted ring, he seized
control of all seven beasts. Thus did the

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:39.941
<v Beezle Wheezelby>company proceed through the streets of
Fornost accompanied by a most unusual

00:06:39.941 --> 00:06:40.799
<v Beezle Wheezelby>procession.

00:06:41.225 --> 00:06:46.790
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Before long, they encountered eight
rough-looking fellows armed with clubs

00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:47.705
<v Beezle Wheezelby>and daggers.

00:06:48.046 --> 00:06:53.994
<v Beezle Wheezelby>The strangers demanded the party's money
and warned them to remove their peculiar

00:06:53.994 --> 00:06:54.366
<v Beezle Wheezelby>pets.

00:06:54.815 --> 00:06:57.215
<v Beezle Wheezelby>The adventurers declined.

00:06:57.692 --> 00:07:02.252
<v Beezle Wheezelby>It was then discovered that the would-be
robbers were—dwarves!

00:07:02.658 --> 00:07:04.978
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Battle erupted in the alley!

00:07:05.378 --> 00:07:10.584
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Sigurd and Karl fought with steel, while
Sulde unleashed his rats upon the

00:07:10.584 --> 00:07:16.146
<v Beezle Wheezelby>attackers. Small though they were, the
creatures swarmed the dwarves, biting at

00:07:16.146 --> 00:07:21.138
<v Beezle Wheezelby>their ankles and leaping upon their
faces. Several rats perished in the

00:07:21.138 --> 00:07:24.418
<v Beezle Wheezelby>struggle, but their interference proved
useful.

00:07:24.947 --> 00:07:30.168
<v Beezle Wheezelby>As the dwarves began to retreat, Sigurd
seized one of them and hurled him bodily

00:07:30.168 --> 00:07:34.067
<v Beezle Wheezelby>back toward his companions, knocking the
fellow unconscious.

00:07:34.589 --> 00:07:40.599
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Alok, attempting a similar capture, found
himself caught in a dwarven bear hug. Yet

00:07:40.599 --> 00:07:45.069
<v Beezle Wheezelby>he escaped the embrace, and the company
pressed its advantage.

00:07:45.537 --> 00:07:51.140
<v Beezle Wheezelby>When the fighting ended, three dwarves
lay dead, three had been taken prisoner,

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:52.577
<v Beezle Wheezelby>and two had escaped.

00:07:52.985 --> 00:07:57.385
<v Beezle Wheezelby>The captives were questioned about the
illegal mining operations.

00:07:57.899 --> 00:08:02.820
<v Beezle Wheezelby>One admitted that the kingdom in the
northwestern mountains had indeed been

00:08:02.820 --> 00:08:07.408
<v Beezle Wheezelby>sending miners and appraisers into
Guthrie's territory. Supplies moved

00:08:07.408 --> 00:08:12.728
<v Beezle Wheezelby>secretly to their outposts, and the trade
was apparently well known among dwarves

00:08:12.728 --> 00:08:13.659
<v Beezle Wheezelby>in the region.

00:08:14.072 --> 00:08:18.712
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Here, at last, was something more
substantial than rumor.

00:08:19.169 --> 00:08:24.418
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Unfortunately, the town guard arrived to
find the adventurers standing beside

00:08:24.418 --> 00:08:27.249
<v Beezle Wheezelby>several corpses, searching their pockets.

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:30.060
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Explanations were required.

00:08:30.512 --> 00:08:36.607
<v Beezle Wheezelby>There followed many hours of questioning,
paperwork, and the dull machinery of

00:08:36.607 --> 00:08:38.032
<v Beezle Wheezelby>civilized justice.

00:08:38.404 --> 00:08:44.213
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Eventually, the company was released, and
the prisoners remained in custody. Sigurd

00:08:44.213 --> 00:08:47.684
<v Beezle Wheezelby>brought news of their discoveries to Lord
Guthrie.

00:08:48.099 --> 00:08:52.885
<v Beezle Wheezelby>The lord was less impressed by the
capture of street ruffians than by the

00:08:52.885 --> 00:08:57.139
<v Beezle Wheezelby>possibility of finally striking at the
illicit mining operations.

00:08:57.611 --> 00:09:02.251
<v Beezle Wheezelby>He agreed to lend the company a spearman
for their next expedition.

00:09:02.656 --> 00:09:07.803
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Thus, armed with fresh evidence, an
additional soldier, and a somewhat

00:09:07.803 --> 00:09:13.100
<v Beezle Wheezelby>diminished collection of rats, the
adventurers prepared to return to the

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:14.816
<v Beezle Wheezelby>burial mound of Yarbon.

00:09:15.302 --> 00:09:21.362
<v Beezle Wheezelby><break time="0.9s"/>Part III: Beneath
Yarbon's Mound.<break time="1.4s"/>

00:09:21.472 --> 00:09:26.974
<v Beezle Wheezelby>On the twenty-ninth day of October, the
company traveled once more into the

00:09:26.974 --> 00:09:27.792
<v Beezle Wheezelby>wilderness.

00:09:28.136 --> 00:09:34.024
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Their path carried them through open
grasslands and into the blackened remains

00:09:34.024 --> 00:09:39.529
<v Beezle Wheezelby>of a forest that had suffered a great
fire. Beyond the burned trees stood

00:09:39.529 --> 00:09:45.341
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Yarbon's burial mound, a vast earthen
monument whose ancient silence had been

00:09:45.341 --> 00:09:47.176
<v Beezle Wheezelby>disturbed by excavation.

00:09:47.496 --> 00:09:53.734
<v Beezle Wheezelby>There, beneath the hill, lay passages of
worked stone, forgotten chambers, and the

00:09:53.734 --> 00:09:55.736
<v Beezle Wheezelby>workings of secret miners.

00:09:56.250 --> 00:10:01.808
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Theophrastus, a gnome skilled in the arts
of thievery, joined the company, while

00:10:01.808 --> 00:10:06.170
<v Beezle Wheezelby>the mounted crossbowmen remained above to
guard their supplies.

00:10:06.702 --> 00:10:09.902
<v Beezle Wheezelby>The others descended into the darkness.

00:10:10.362 --> 00:10:13.562
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Their first discovery was an unsettling
one.

00:10:14.022 --> 00:10:19.553
<v Beezle Wheezelby>A chamber they had visited before was now
locked, and when its door was forced

00:10:19.553 --> 00:10:23.862
<v Beezle Wheezelby>open, two shambling corpses lurched
forward to strike Sigurd.

00:10:24.317 --> 00:10:26.877
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Their blows failed to find him.

00:10:27.429 --> 00:10:33.658
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Sulde raised his unholy power against the
undead, and the creatures fell under its

00:10:33.658 --> 00:10:37.349
<v Beezle Wheezelby>influence, wandering aimlessly about the
chamber.

00:10:37.751 --> 00:10:39.911
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Yet something was amiss.

00:10:40.366 --> 00:10:45.973
<v Beezle Wheezelby>The room had changed since the company's
previous visit. A wooden table and chairs

00:10:45.973 --> 00:10:50.126
<v Beezle Wheezelby>had appeared, and an empty drinking glass
lay upon the table.

00:10:50.635 --> 00:10:52.635
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Someone had been here.

00:10:53.172 --> 00:10:57.492
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Someone living, perhaps, who held little
fear of the dead.

00:10:57.903 --> 00:11:00.943
<v Beezle Wheezelby>The adventurers chose not to linger.

00:11:01.328 --> 00:11:06.673
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Instead, they passed deeper into the
mound, through a hidden stone entrance

00:11:06.673 --> 00:11:08.768
<v Beezle Wheezelby>opened by a chain and pulley.

00:11:09.168 --> 00:11:15.241
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Beyond lay an extensive network of mining
tunnels. Sigurd employed a magical wand

00:11:15.241 --> 00:11:21.238
<v Beezle Wheezelby>capable of detecting precious metals, and
the company found faint traces of gold

00:11:21.238 --> 00:11:22.528
<v Beezle Wheezelby>within the stone.

00:11:23.094 --> 00:11:28.291
<v Beezle Wheezelby>They also discovered a great shaft
descending into darkness, with a wooden

00:11:28.291 --> 00:11:30.854
<v Beezle Wheezelby>lifting platform suspended above it.

00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:37.601
<v Beezle Wheezelby>From far below came indistinct sounds, as
though tools were striking against the

00:11:37.601 --> 00:11:38.070
<v Beezle Wheezelby>earth.

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:43.588
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Whatever work had been done in these
tunnels, it seemed the miners had not

00:11:43.588 --> 00:11:44.220
<v Beezle Wheezelby>finished.

00:11:44.602 --> 00:11:49.251
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Beyond the great lifting shaft, the
adventurers found a small chamber

00:11:49.251 --> 00:11:52.122
<v Beezle Wheezelby>containing four boarded holes in the
floor.

00:11:52.546 --> 00:11:55.986
<v Beezle Wheezelby>In one corner lay a weathered leather
case.

00:11:56.415 --> 00:12:00.895
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Sigurd retrieved it, and from within drew
a faded parchment.

00:12:01.434 --> 00:12:03.354
<v Beezle Wheezelby>It was a treasure map.

00:12:03.788 --> 00:12:09.916
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Upon examining its markings, the company
realized that it pointed not to the mines

00:12:09.916 --> 00:12:15.665
<v Beezle Wheezelby>beneath their feet, but to a mountain
west of Oroth's fortress. There, on the

00:12:15.665 --> 00:12:21.263
<v Beezle Wheezelby>mountain's far side, a hidden treasure
was said to lie buried within a deep

00:12:21.263 --> 00:12:21.868
<v Beezle Wheezelby>crevice.

00:12:22.338 --> 00:12:25.618
<v Beezle Wheezelby>A new mystery had been placed before
them.

00:12:26.024 --> 00:12:30.744
<v Beezle Wheezelby>But for the moment, their attention
returned to the holes in the floor.

00:12:31.278 --> 00:12:36.862
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Three were narrow shafts. The fourth was
wide enough for a man to descend, and an

00:12:36.862 --> 00:12:41.678
<v Beezle Wheezelby>iron ring beside it suggested that ropes
had once been fastened there.

00:12:42.096 --> 00:12:46.016
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Sigurd cast a burning torch into the
darkness.

00:12:46.462 --> 00:12:52.178
<v Beezle Wheezelby>It fell some forty feet before a terrible
screech rose from below. In the

00:12:52.178 --> 00:12:56.782
<v Beezle Wheezelby>flickering light, a long black leg passed
across the shaft.

00:12:57.254 --> 00:12:59.974
<v Beezle Wheezelby>The company considered its options.

00:13:00.496 --> 00:13:02.496
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Then came the fire.

00:13:02.929 --> 00:13:09.089
<v Beezle Wheezelby>A flask of burning oil was hurled into
the pit. Flame roared upward, scorching

00:13:09.089 --> 00:13:15.329
<v Beezle Wheezelby>the air and destroying the webs below.
The hideous screeching grew louder, then

00:13:15.329 --> 00:13:15.809
<v Beezle Wheezelby>faded.

00:13:16.281 --> 00:13:21.578
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Believing the danger reduced, the
adventurers lowered Alok into the shaft

00:13:21.578 --> 00:13:22.681
<v Beezle Wheezelby>to investigate.

00:13:23.076 --> 00:13:28.657
<v Beezle Wheezelby>He discovered the charred remains of
large spiders and the ruined webbing of

00:13:28.657 --> 00:13:29.476
<v Beezle Wheezelby>their nest.

00:13:29.949 --> 00:13:32.749
<v Beezle Wheezelby>But not all the creatures had perished.

00:13:33.296 --> 00:13:39.255
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Several surviving spiders crawled along
the walls toward the dangling ranger. His

00:13:39.255 --> 00:13:44.692
<v Beezle Wheezelby>companions hauled him upward, yet not
before one beast struck and sank its

00:13:44.692 --> 00:13:46.256
<v Beezle Wheezelby>venom into his flesh.

00:13:46.778 --> 00:13:53.144
<v Beezle Wheezelby>The poison was weak, but insidious. It
would sap his strength slowly as time

00:13:53.144 --> 00:13:53.738
<v Beezle Wheezelby>passed.

00:13:54.122 --> 00:13:59.844
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Alok survived the bite, though the danger
of remaining beneath the earth had grown

00:13:59.844 --> 00:14:00.762
<v Beezle Wheezelby>considerably.

00:14:01.126 --> 00:14:04.726
<v Beezle Wheezelby>The company debated whether to retreat
immediately.

00:14:05.074 --> 00:14:11.370
<v Beezle Wheezelby>And, as so often happens when treasure
and curiosity are involved, they decided

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:14.034
<v Beezle Wheezelby>to examine just one more chamber.

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:20.700
<v Beezle Wheezelby><break time="0.9s"/>Part IV: The Dwarves
and Their Gold.<break time="1.4s"/>

00:14:20.808 --> 00:14:25.768
<v Beezle Wheezelby>The chamber held precisely the sort of
company they had come to find.

00:14:26.166 --> 00:14:32.425
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Six dwarves stood within: three miners
bearing heavy pickaxes, and three armed

00:14:32.425 --> 00:14:36.246
<v Beezle Wheezelby>guards. Two of the guards carried a large
chest.

00:14:36.723 --> 00:14:39.283
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Both parties saw one another.

00:14:39.652 --> 00:14:45.347
<v Beezle Wheezelby>There would be no ambush, no easy
concealment, and little opportunity for

00:14:45.347 --> 00:14:46.692
<v Beezle Wheezelby>misunderstanding.

00:14:47.126 --> 00:14:50.006
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Sigurd and his companions attacked.

00:14:50.473 --> 00:14:55.652
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Bolts and arrows flew through the chamber
as the warriors closed the distance.

00:14:55.652 --> 00:15:01.033
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Their dogs leapt upon the miners, and in
the first rush of combat all three fell.

00:15:01.474 --> 00:15:06.437
<v Beezle Wheezelby>The guards, enraged by the deaths of
their companions, abandoned their burden

00:15:06.437 --> 00:15:07.874
<v Beezle Wheezelby>and drew their swords.

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:10.640
<v Beezle Wheezelby>The battle grew fierce.

00:15:11.094 --> 00:15:17.274
<v Beezle Wheezelby>One dog suffered a grievous wound. Sigurd
himself was struck, and in the confusion

00:15:17.274 --> 00:15:22.614
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Sulde's curse fell not upon the enemy
alone, but upon Alok's own hound.

00:15:23.087 --> 00:15:27.087
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Yet the dwarven guards could not
withstand the onslaught.

00:15:27.505 --> 00:15:32.865
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Two were slain, and the last, wounded and
surrounded, surrendered.

00:15:33.281 --> 00:15:37.441
<v Beezle Wheezelby>This time the company took care to
preserve a prisoner.

00:15:37.882 --> 00:15:43.251
<v Beezle Wheezelby>The chest proved to contain a large
nugget of nearly pure gold, valued at

00:15:43.251 --> 00:15:48.546
<v Beezle Wheezelby>roughly one hundred and thirty gold
pieces, together with heavy rocks of

00:15:48.546 --> 00:15:53.765
<v Beezle Wheezelby>gold-bearing ore. Another forty gold
pieces were found among the fallen

00:15:53.765 --> 00:15:54.362
<v Beezle Wheezelby>dwarves.

00:15:54.865 --> 00:16:00.546
<v Beezle Wheezelby>At last, the hidden mining operation had
yielded proof that could be carried into

00:16:00.546 --> 00:16:01.185
<v Beezle Wheezelby>daylight.

00:16:01.556 --> 00:16:06.762
<v Beezle Wheezelby>With a prisoner in chains and treasure in
hand, the company retraced its steps

00:16:06.762 --> 00:16:11.698
<v Beezle Wheezelby>through the tunnels. They passed the
silent room of the undead, locked the

00:16:11.698 --> 00:16:16.836
<v Beezle Wheezelby>great iron door behind them, and emerged
from the mound into the evening air.

00:16:17.363 --> 00:16:22.883
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Alok's poison had taken its toll, but its
effects had finally ceased.

00:16:23.218 --> 00:16:28.178
<v Beezle Wheezelby>They made camp away from the mound,
guarding their captive through the night.

00:16:28.524 --> 00:16:32.684
<v Beezle Wheezelby>And for once, the darkness passed without
incident.

00:16:33.099 --> 00:16:38.919
<v Beezle Wheezelby><break time="0.9s"/>Part V: The Return to
Fornost.<break time="1.4s"/>

00:16:39.034 --> 00:16:43.354
<v Beezle Wheezelby>The following morning, the adventurers
began their journey home.

00:16:43.713 --> 00:16:49.386
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Their passage was slower now, burdened
with a prisoner, wounded companions, and

00:16:49.386 --> 00:16:50.913
<v Beezle Wheezelby>the spoils of battle.

00:16:51.422 --> 00:16:56.943
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Along the forest's edge, they encountered
a patrol of seven knights in the service

00:16:56.943 --> 00:17:01.987
<v Beezle Wheezelby>of Lord Guthrie. Some recognized Sigurd
from earlier training, and when the

00:17:01.987 --> 00:17:07.371
<v Beezle Wheezelby>company explained the prisoner and the
stolen gold, the knights agreed to escort

00:17:07.371 --> 00:17:08.462
<v Beezle Wheezelby>them to Fornost.

00:17:09.006 --> 00:17:14.315
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Thus they returned not as wandering
treasure hunters, but under armed escort,

00:17:14.315 --> 00:17:18.366
<v Beezle Wheezelby>bearing evidence of a trespass against
their lord's domain.

00:17:18.883 --> 00:17:22.803
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Guthrie received them and examined their
prisoner.

00:17:23.222 --> 00:17:29.053
<v Beezle Wheezelby>The dwarf had grown silent, unwilling to
reveal what he knew. But the lord seemed

00:17:29.053 --> 00:17:33.062
<v Beezle Wheezelby>confident that the man's secrets could
yet be uncovered.

00:17:33.439 --> 00:17:38.807
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Pleased with the company's success,
Guthrie awarded them an additional three

00:17:38.807 --> 00:17:40.239
<v Beezle Wheezelby>hundred gold pieces.

00:17:40.678 --> 00:17:46.614
<v Beezle Wheezelby>And so, by the afternoon of October the
thirtieth, their venture had come to an

00:17:46.614 --> 00:17:46.918
<v Beezle Wheezelby>end.

00:17:47.342 --> 00:17:52.622
<v Beezle Wheezelby>There was gold to divide, wounds to mend,
and much to consider.

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:57.984
<v Beezle Wheezelby>For they had entered the wilderness
seeking wolf pups, and returned having

00:17:57.984 --> 00:18:03.401
<v Beezle Wheezelby>uncovered the workings of a hidden mine,
captured servants of a secretive dwarven

00:18:03.401 --> 00:18:07.600
<v Beezle Wheezelby>enterprise, and discovered a map to yet
another buried fortune.

00:18:08.142 --> 00:18:10.622
<v Beezle Wheezelby>But many questions remained.

00:18:11.071 --> 00:18:16.368
<v Beezle Wheezelby>Who had furnished the chamber of the
walking dead? How deep did the dwarven

00:18:16.368 --> 00:18:22.094
<v Beezle Wheezelby>excavations descend? What lay beyond the
wooden lift? And what treasure waited in

00:18:22.094 --> 00:18:24.671
<v Beezle Wheezelby>the crevice beyond Oroth's fortress?

00:18:25.206 --> 00:18:27.926
<v Beezle Wheezelby>These were matters for another journey.

00:18:28.396 --> 00:18:34.427
<v Beezle Wheezelby>For gold has a way of drawing men into
the darkest places of the world. And more

00:18:34.427 --> 00:18:40.076
<v Beezle Wheezelby>often than not, those places were dark
long before the gold was ever found.

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:44.680
<v Beezle Wheezelby>So ends this chapter of the adventurers
of Fornost.

00:18:45.147 --> 00:18:50.668
<v Beezle Wheezelby>They had survived wolves, thieves, the
walking dead, venomous spiders, and the

00:18:50.668 --> 00:18:52.747
<v Beezle Wheezelby>servants of a hidden kingdom.

00:18:53.248 --> 00:18:58.208
<v Beezle Wheezelby>And somewhere beneath the earth, the
miners' secrets still waited.

